<Base title="Privacy and consent" description="What EskeeWalker Strategies collects through its forms and tools, why, where it is stored, and how to withdraw consent.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
  <h1>Privacy and consent.</h1>
  <p>This page is the notice behind every form and tool on this site, written for India's Digital Personal Data Protection rules.</p>
  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>Your name, work email, phone number if you give it, company name, and what you write in the form or answer in a tool. From email, we also record whether a message was delivered, opened or replied to.</p>
  <h2>Why</h2>
  <p>To reply to your enquiry, keep track of the conversation, send you the result of a tool you used, and, with your tick-box consent, send occasional notes on strategy and growth. Nothing else.</p>
  <h2>Where it is stored</h2>
  <p>In our own CRM and email system on a server in India run by EskeeWalker Strategies LLP, Jaipur. We do not sell or share it. Email is delivered through a sending service; it sees the address and the message, as any postal service would.</p>
  <h2>How to withdraw</h2>
  <p>Reply "unsubscribe" to any email, use the unsubscribe link in any email, or write to us. We stop at once and keep a record that you asked, which is the only reason we keep the address after that.</p>
  <h2>The consent wording we store</h2>
  <p>We keep the exact text you agreed to, the time, and the page, so we can show it if asked.</p>
</Base>
